<title>GERMANY: German Feb trade surplus rises to 9.2 bln DM.</title>
<headline>German Feb trade surplus rises to 9.2 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator (bln marks):</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC  Feb 97   Jan 97	  Feb 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		 +9.2     +5.6	    +8.4</p>
<p> Current account	     -1.5     -9.8	    +0.6</p>
<p> Exports			 67.8     64.4	    62.9</p>
<p> Imports			 58.6     58.8	    54.5</p>
<p> Services			-4.1     -5.6	    -2.4</p>
<p> Wage and property income  -1.3     -5.4	    -0.9</p>
<p> Transfers		     -5.2     -4.1	    -4.4</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	 -0.1     -0.3	    -0.1</p>
<p>GERMAN TRADE/CURRENT ACC Jan-Feb 97     Jan-Feb 96</p>
<p> Trade balance		  +14.8	     +13.0</p>
<p> Current account		-11.2	     - 3.4</p>
<p> Exports			  132.2	     124.2</p>
<p> Imports			  117.4	     111.2</p>
<p> Services			 - 9.6	     - 6.7</p>
<p> Wage and property income   - 6.7	     - 2.4</p>
<p> Transfers			- 9.3	     - 6.3</p>
<p> Supplementary trade	  - 0.4	     - 1.0</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
